# SVN revision diff
# Source: https://svn.code.sf.net/p/civ4betterai/code/
# Revision: 119
# Author: iustus
# Date: 2006-11-25T06:13:51.347594Z
# Coverage: full
# Message:
#   findPopulationRank, findBaseYieldRateRank, findYieldRateRank, findCommerceRateRank all cached, they can now be called more liberally without performance penalties
#   getBuildingCommerceByBuilding cleaned up so that it does less work when commerce is going to be zero
#   AI_commerceWeight now reflects whether the player is going for a cultural victory, all the places that called this and then adjusted for cultural victory outside the call were adjusted
#   AI_specialistValue removed the 'hack' to prefer merchants if you emphasized commerce, now it picks each commerce type based on the player's commerce slider allocations (so if you doing 80% research, 10% culture, 10% gold and emph commerce, then you get 80% emph on research, 10% emph on gold, and 10% emph on culture, so scientists will get a boost, if the slider is moved to all culture, then artists will have the biggest boost)
#   if a city needs to pop borders (its culture level is under 2), we now will run culture process correctly in the case where we captured the city (in that case, the culture level is 1)
#   otherwise, if we just captured a city, and it is still in revolt, we will pick a building (food, production, then anything) rather than a unit
#   National and World wonders will be more likely to be built in appropriate cities (if its not the top 4 rank of whatever the wonder does, it gets low value)
#   Buildings that increase great people rate are more likely to be built in cities that already have a high great person rate
#   monastaries are more likely to be built under cultural victory strategy, or in the early game (more than 1 era prior to obselecence)
#   under cultural victory strat, temples are given high priority if there are not enough yet built to get a cathedral in the top 3 culture cities
#   we make sure we build cathedrals in the top culture cities first 
#   possible crash because parameters of DLLExport'ed AI_processValue removed, now we overload the function to add parameter
#   AI_processValue gives higher priority to culture process if we need to pop borders, also under cultural victory
#   AI_forceEmphasizeCulture added, since there is no EmphasizeInfo in XML to do this. This works just like regular emphasize calls, except it does not have an associated EmphasizeInfo
#   we now call AI_forceEmphasizeCulture(true) on the top 4 culture cities in cultural victory strat
#   we cache the number of cities needed for cultural victory, culturalVictoryNumCultureCities - you can also call culturalVictoryValid which uses the same cached value (zero means cultural victory is not valid)
#   limitedWonderClassLimit added, since isLimitedWonderClass does not specify how many you can build. this new function returns the number you can build (it adds up the numbers of each type, although in the default XML there are no wonders that are both national and world, but it is possible)
#   alt mouseover city under chipotle cheat mode shows the ranks for population, yields, commerce
#   alt mouseover player under chipotle cheat mode (which shows attitude) also shows if in financial trouble
#   getBuildingClassPrereqBuilding does almost zero work in the case where it is going to return zero
#   AI_religionValue does less work when it is going to return zero
#   if we get to cultural victory stage 2, dagger strat is forced off
#   AI_getBestGroupAttacker does less work when bForce is true
#   AI_sumStrength works correctly in the case where you need to declare war to move into the plot to be attacked
#   canMoveInto: check on !isHuman() removed when you would need to declareWar to move. Previously it would return false in this case. There is a temporary assert there now, to see when this happens. Currently it only seems to happen on sea-going exploring units and the case we wanted to catch, when a unit needs to attack to move into territory where it wants to declare war. 
#   divide by zero crash fixed when improper units were given great people missions (discover value would be zero)
#   AI_stackAttackCity now passes (bDeclareWar = true) to canMoveInto and (bPotentialEnemy = true) to AI_compareStacks
#   
